          "anchorId": "grand-pricks",
          "heading": "Grand Pricks",
          "body": "The Grand Pricks are the self-anointed elite of the asphalt, treating every Tuesday morning commute like it’s the final lap at Monaco. These villains are perpetually in a state of high-velocity desperation, fueled by the delusion that they can actually \"win\" at traffic. While they possess heavy feet and even heavier egos, their tactical execution is consistently undermined by their own stubbornness. To a Grand Prick, the highway isn't a public utility—it’s a podium, and they are currently in P1 (even if they’re actually just stuck behind a school bus).\n\nYou don't need a radar gun to spot these villains; you just need to look for the driver whose blood pressure is visibly higher than their tire pressure.\n\nThe Grand Pricks are the most stressed inhabitants of the Rush Hour Villains universe, who are trapped in a cycle of perpetual fury. Their tragedy lies in the math: they exert 100% more effort for a 0% increase in arrival time. They are the architects of their own frustration, forever chasing a checkered flag that is actually just a \"Road Work Ahead\" sign.",
