          "background": "dark",
          "anchorId": "slow-moes",
          "heading": "Slow Moes",
          "body": "The Slow Moes are the highway’s premier practitioners of automotive meditation. To this clan, the \"limit\" in \"speed limit\" is an aspirational goal they have no intention of reaching. While other villains are defined by their aggression or their vanity, the Slow Moes are defined by their absolute, glacial laziness. They are the primary architects of the \"phantom traffic jam\"—that mysterious phenomenon where traffic grinds to a halt for three miles, only for everyone to eventually pass a single, beige sedan cruising at the speed of a brisk walk.\n\nDetecting a Slow Moe requires patience, a full tank of gas, and perhaps a stress ball. You can find them at the very front of every line of frustrated cars on the planet.\n\nThe Slow Moes represent the ultimate friction in the Rush Hour Villains ecosystem. They are the antithesis of the Grand Pricks; where the Pricks seek to win the race, the Moes have forgotten the race even started. They aren't just \"not in a hurry\"—they are fundamentally opposed to the concept of arrival. Within the Official Survival Guide, they are classified as the most dangerous type of passive-aggressive obstacle. By weaponizing their own lethargy, they ensure that the \"rush\" is removed from \"rush hour,\" leaving only the \"hour\" (and usually a second one) for everyone stuck behind them.",
          "imagePath": "clans/slowmoes.png",
          "imagePosition": "left",
          "imageMaxWidth": "300",
          "cta_linkType": "none",
          "cta_linkUrl": "home",
